    <string name="info_active_algorithm">The algorithm whose clicks run after the next round. A low coefficient moves on to the next one, a high one goes back to Algorithm 1.</string>
    <string name="info_balance_control">Protects the balance: stops or pauses monitoring and clicks when the internet is too slow for the game, and (with the guarded start) checks the balance on the screen at the start and after every round.</string>
    <string name="info_guarded">The algorithms stake only after a number of low coefficients (≤ threshold) in a row. The amount is split into parts: when a part is made, everything goes back to Algorithm 1 and waits for lows again; after the last part everything stops. Stakes follow from the threshold, so that a win brings back what was lost since the last win plus start stake × (threshold − 1). A run of lows does not change the chance of the next round.</string>
    <string name="info_last_ocr">The text last read in the newest tile. Useful when a round is not recognised.</string>
    <string name="info_last_round">The last coefficient read from the game and what it did to the sequence.</string>
    <string name="info_notifications">Needed for the monitoring notification with pause and stop, and for alerts.</string>
    <string name="info_ocr_status">What the screen reading is doing now: searching for the row, reading, waiting for a tile to settle, or OK. The percentage is the reading confidence.</string>
    <string name="info_recent_events">The last rounds processed. The full list with search and export is in Log.</string>
    <string name="info_recovery">Use these if the sequence got out of step with the game.</string>
    <string name="info_row">Where the coefficient row is on the screen. Monitoring finds it by itself and follows it when the game scrolls; Find row looks for it again right away.</string>
    <string name="info_threshold">The coefficient you set (now %1$s). After each round: if the round\'s coefficient is %1$s or lower, the next algorithm runs; if it is higher, the sequence goes back to Algorithm 1.</string>
